STRUCTURED PICO EXTRACTION FOR CHAP TRIAL:                                                                              
                                                                                                                        
**Study Identification:**                                                                                               
- Title: Cotrimoxazole as prophylaxis against opportunistic infections in HIV-infected Zambian children (CHAP): a       
double-blind randomised placebo-controlled trial                                                                        
- Citation: Kazembe et al. 2004 (CHAP trial)                                                                            
- Study Design: Double-blind randomised placebo-controlled trial (RCT)                                                  
- Study Index: 1                                                                                                        
                                                                                                                        
**Population:**                                                                                                         
- Inclusion: Children aged 1-14 years with clinical features of HIV infection in Zambia                                 
- Sample size: 541 children randomly assigned; 7 excluded (HIV negative); 534 HIV-infected children analyzed            
- Setting: Zambia (resource-poor setting with high bacterial resistance to cotrimoxazole)                               
                                                                                                                        
**Intervention:**                                                                                                       
- Daily co-trimoxazole (trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole) prophylaxis                                                      
- Regimen: Continuous daily administration                                                                              
                                                                                                                        
**Comparison:**                                                                                                         
- Matching placebo (double-blind randomised placebo-controlled trial)                                                   
- Analysis method: Intention-to-treat                                                                                   
                                                                                                                        
**Outcomes with Results:**                                                                                              
                                                                                                                        
1. ALL-CAUSE MORTALITY (Primary Outcome):                                                                               
   - Co-trimoxazole: 74 deaths (28%)                                                                                    
   - Placebo: 112 deaths (42%)                                                                                          
   - Effect measure: Hazard Ratio (HR) = 0.57                                                                           
   - 95% CI: 0.43 to 0.77                                                                                               
   - p-value: 0.0002                                                                                                    
                                                                                                                        
2. MORTALITY BEYOND 12 MONTHS FOLLOW-UP:                                                                                
   - Effect measure: HR = 0.48                                                                                          
   - 95% CI: 0.27 to 0.84                                                                                               
   - Test for heterogeneity: p=0.60                                                                                     
   - Number analyzed: 320 children                                                                                      
                                                                                                                        
3. GRADE 3 OR 4 ADVERSE EVENTS:                                                                                         
   - Co-trimoxazole group: 16 (6%)                                                                                      
   - Placebo group: 18 (7%)                                                                                             
   - No significant difference                                                                                          
                                                                                                                        
4. NEUTROPENIA (neutrophil count <0.5 × 10^9/L):                                                                        
   - Co-trimoxazole: 16 (6%)                                                                                            
   - Placebo: 7 (3%)                                                                                                    
   - p-value: 0.06 (borderline significant)                                                                             
                                                                                                                        
5. PNEUMOCYSTIS CARINII PNEUMONIA:                                                                                      
   - Only 1 case identified (in placebo group) among 73 nasopharyngeal aspirates from children with pneumonia           
                                                                                                                        
