- Age: No heterogeneity (p=0.82) - benefit consistent across all ages                                                   
- Baseline CD4 counts: No heterogeneity (p=0.36) - benefit consistent across all immune status levels                   
                                                                                                                        
**Follow-up:**                                                                                                          
- Median follow-up: 19 months                                                                                           
- Trial stopped early in October 2003 by data and safety monitoring committee due to clear mortality benefit            
                                                                                                                        
**Adverse Events Summary:**                                                                                             
- Serious adverse events (grade 3-4): 6% vs 7% (NS)                                                                     
- Rash: Minimal occurrence (one case in placebo)                                                                        
- Neutropenia: Slightly higher in treatment group (6% vs 3%, p=0.06)                                                    
                                                                                                                        
**Key Clinical Implications:**                                                                                          
1. 43% reduction in mortality with co-trimoxazole prophylaxis                                                           
2. Benefit applies to ALL ages and CD4 count categories                                                                 
3. Acceptable safety profile - no excess serious adverse events                                                         
4. Recommendation: All HIV-infected children in resource-poor settings should receive co-trimoxazole prophylaxis        
regardless of local resistance patterns                                                                                 
                                                                                                                        
### 3. Additional context:                                                                                              
This CHAP trial was a landmark study addressing the question of whether co-trimoxazole prophylaxis would be effective in
areas with high bacterial resistance. The results convincingly showed that prophylaxis remains highly effective even in 
such settings. The trial was stopped early for efficacy due to the overwhelming mortality benefit observed. This        
